{# icons - the brand-agnostic LINE-ICON vocabulary (the closed set defined in
   docs/ROLE-DEVICE-CONTRACT.md, "THE ICON VOCABULARY").

   The writer picks a SEMANTIC KEY (zeit, geld, person, ...); the renderer owns
   the drawing. One macro, `icon(key, uid)`, returns an inline 24x24 <svg> that
   inherits its colour from the host via stroke="currentColor", so an icon is
   never a brand literal and never needs a token of its own: it takes whatever
   colour its card sets. NO external icon library, NO icon webfont (a webfont
   glyph cannot be embedded reliably in the print head, see icon_array's note in
   viz_proportion.jinja), pure inline geometry.

   House style: thin, geometric, calm. Circles, lines, and short paths only,
   fill="none" + a single 1.6 stroke, round caps and joins, drawn on the 24 grid
   with a ~2 unit optical margin so every glyph sits on the same visual weight.

   Graceful: an unknown, empty, or missing key renders NOTHING (never a broken
   glyph, never a fallback box). That keeps `icon` safe to call unconditionally,
   so a card can always ask for its icon and simply get nothing back.

   uid is accepted for signature parity with the viz macros (the dispatch threads
   loop.index). These glyphs deliberately define NO ids, gradients, or clip
   paths, so two equal icons on one page cannot collide by construction. #}

